C03: a deictic «look at it and say what it is» with no antecedent asks what to look at (DIALOGUE1487)

«Quiero que lo veas y de que se trata?» (H0528) reached no reader and went to the model as conversation. `_standalone_deictic_request` now reads a request to look at «lo/esto/eso» (miralo, fijate, velo, look at it, check it) optionally followed by «y decime de qué se trata / qué es / what it's about», with no previous request in the history, as a bare deictic order without an object; the turn answers with the missing-referent clarifier already used for «abrí eso» — one short question with the same verb, no guess.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


